  "_comment": "Hand-authored launch puzzles. Every word is a concrete, common noun that a good clue can reach without the blocked routes. The banned list is the five most obvious paths to the word — that constraint is the entire game, so these were chosen by asking 'what would I write first?' and blocking exactly that.",
  "_rules": [
    "Concrete nouns only. Abstractions ('freedom') make the machine's guess unfalsifiable.",
    "No proper nouns, no brands. They tempt the model into trivia rather than inference.",
    "5 banned words each: block the category, the defining feature, and the 3 nearest synonyms.",
    "A banned word must never contain the secret word or vice versa — the generator checks this.",
    "Difficulty 1-5 is a guess here; the generator overwrites it with a real solve simulation.",
    "allow[] whitelists words the substring filter wrongly catches. Populate it from probe-validator.mjs, never by guessing."
  ],
